1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,010
Listen to a talk on environmental conservation.

2
00:00:03,010 --> 00:00:07,220
Let's talk the environmental issue that has to do with how common household products have changed.

3
00:00:07,220 --> 00:00:11,640
More and more products contain bacterial killing chemicals these days.

4
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:16,059
These antibacterial chemicals aren't just in product like soap.

5
00:00:16,059 --> 00:00:18,553
They are in all sorts of household cleaners and toothpaste.

6
00:00:18,553 --> 00:00:24,290
And if you think about it for second you will realize that most of those chemicals just end up going down the drain.

7
00:00:24,290 --> 00:00:29,733
But you are probably thinking that all that stuff go through a treatment plan that removes chemicals, right?

8
00:00:29,733 --> 00:00:33,966
After all that's what happens to stuff that goes down the drain Well,

9
00:00:33,966 --> 00:00:38,502
waste water is treated, but that doesn't usually remove all the chemicals in it.

10
00:00:38,502 --> 00:00:42,130
The chemicals left in the treated water get into the aquatic environment.

11
00:00:42,130 --> 00:00:47,070
That is into the rivers, and streams where plants and fish and other animals live.

12
00:00:47,070 --> 00:00:51,339
Now to find out the effect of antibacterial chemicals on freshwater ecosystems,

13
00:00:51,339 --> 00:00:55,280
a study was done with algae, which are tiny plant-like organisms.

14
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:58,197
Different species of algae were taken to a lab

15
00:00:58,197 --> 00:01:04,030
and then exposed to just a few antibacterial chemicals found in the streams. And guess what?

16
00:01:04,030 --> 00:01:08,548
In the experiment, the overall growth of algae and the number of species dropped.

17
00:01:08,548 --> 00:01:11,130
This is not good and here is why.

18
00:01:11,130 --> 00:01:14,020
Algae are the base of the aquatic food chain

19
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:17,227
which means that other organisms depend on them for food.

20
00:01:17,227 --> 00:01:20,620
So if the chemicals kill algae at the bottom of the food chain

21
00:01:20,980 --> 00:01:23,020
the whole system is being disrupted.
